+3.  **Resampling and Interpolation:** The volume data is resampled using the transformed grid. Linear interpolation (order 1) is commonly used to sample the original volume at the transformed coordinates [Volume Rotation via Affine Transform](11626-volume-rotation-via-affine-transform.md). Boundary conditions are handled by clamping or returning a default value (e.g., 0) for out-of-bounds samples [Volume Rotation via Affine Transform](11626-volume-rotation-via-affine-transform.md).
 
 4.  **Compositing:** Once the data is pixel-aligned, the transformed slices are composited together to form the final image. This often involves converting the warped data into multiple datasets (substance, opacity, gradient) to generate shaded slices before compositing [S1, unofficial].
